WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:03.946
One day a man and his son headed to the market.

2
00:00:03.947 --> 00:00:06.946
They were leading their donkey along the road.

3
00:00:06.947 --> 00:00:10.887
They planned to sell him at the market.

4
00:00:10.888 --> 00:00:13.783
On their way they passed some farmers.

5
00:00:13.784 --> 00:00:19.111
The farmers burst into laughter.

6
00:00:19.112 --> 00:00:23.367
"They're not even riding their donkey!" one said.

7
00:00:23.368 --> 00:00:26.893
"That donkey must be useless!"

8
00:00:26.894 --> 00:00:37.878
"Yes," another said. "How will they ever sell him at the market?"

9
00:00:37.879 --> 00:00:42.141
The father flushed.

10
00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:45.198
"Son, please ride our donkey.

11
00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:50.749
Then no one will laugh at our donkey or us."

12
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:55.066
The son obeyed and climbed up on the donkey's back.

13
00:00:55.067 --> 00:01:00.393
Soon they passed an old woman sitting on a bench.

14
00:01:00.394 --> 00:01:03.963
"How rude!" she said loudly.

15
00:01:03.964 --> 00:01:09.014
"That boy makes his father walk while he rides on their donkey."

16
00:01:09.015 --> 00:01:14.281
The man felt ashamed again.

17
00:01:14.282 --> 00:01:22.992
"Son, get off the donkey. I'll ride him now."

18
00:01:22.993 --> 00:01:26.516
The man and boy continued on their way.

19
00:01:26.517 --> 00:01:29.971
Before long they passed some girls.

20
00:01:29.972 --> 00:01:35.194
"Look at that terrible father!" one whispered.

21
00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:39.175
"He's making his son walk!"

22
00:01:39.176 --> 00:01:43.950
"That boy looks so tired," another girl said.

23
00:01:43.951 --> 00:01:48.092
"He should be riding on the donkey!"

24
00:01:48.093 --> 00:01:52.402
The man groaned.

25
00:01:52.403 --> 00:01:55.006
"Son, how about this?

26
00:01:55.007 --> 00:02:03.400
We'll both ride on the donkey."

27
00:02:03.401 --> 00:02:06.209
Soon they saw a couple.

28
00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:10.715
"That poor donkey!" the wife said.

29
00:02:10.716 --> 00:02:13.445
"Yes!" The husband scowled.

30
00:02:13.446 --> 00:02:18.807
"How cruel! Who makes a donkey carry two people at once?"

31
00:02:18.808 --> 00:02:22.179
The father and son climbed off their donkey.

32
00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:26.494
With a sigh, the man looked at their donkey.

33
00:02:26.495 --> 00:02:29.768
"He does look tired."

34
00:02:29.769 --> 00:02:33.099
"What should we do?" the son asked.

35
00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:37.252
The father thought. "Let's put the donkey on our shoulders.

36
00:02:37.253 --> 00:02:39.865
We'll carry him to the market."

37
00:02:39.866 --> 00:02:44.209
They carefully tied the donkey's legs together.

38
00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:48.837
"This will make it easier to carry him," the father said.

39
00:02:48.838 --> 00:02:55.105
Then they lifted him onto their shoulders.

40
00:02:55.106 --> 00:02:59.658
As they crossed a bridge, loud laughter rang out.

41
00:02:59.659 --> 00:03:05.087
"Ha-ha! They're carrying a donkey!" someone yelled.

42
00:03:05.088 --> 00:03:12.171
"What a silly sight!" another person cried.

43
00:03:12.172 --> 00:03:17.029
The people laughed so loudly, the poor donkey got startled.

44
00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:21.239
He kicked his legs hard and slipped off his owners' shoulders.

45
00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:26.621
With a terrible splash, he fell into the river—and drowned.

46
00:03:26.622 --> 00:03:36.997
The boy burst into sobs. "Oh no! Our donkey!"

47
00:03:36.998 --> 00:03:40.487
The father put his arm around the boy.

48
00:03:40.488 --> 00:03:45.583
"My son, remember this always," he said softly.

49
00:03:45.584 --> 00:03:53.923
"When you try to please everybody, you end up pleasing nobody."

